 Operations',\n Line 18:     CHIEF_MADOTHI: 'Chief Madothi Children\\'s School & Feeding Fund',\n Line 19:     DEFEND_YOUR_FAITH: 'Defend Your Faith Digital eBooks',\n Line 20:     MYTHOLOGY_SUBS: 'Mythology Subscription Engines',\n Line 21:     STEDT_TYRONE: 'STEDT Tyrone Commission Pipelines',\n Line 22:   };\n\n Now, note that in line 12 and 13, we are using angle brackets for type assertion in the useState call.\n\n This is valid in TypeScript when using JSX? \n But note: in a .tsx file, the angle brackets are not allowed for type assertion because they conflict with JSX.\n We must use the `as` syntax for type assertion in .tsx files.\n\n Ah! This is the problem.\n\n In a .tsx file, we cannot use the angle bracket syntax for type assertion because it is confused with JSX.\n\n We must change:\n\n   const [context, setContext] = useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP');\n\n to\n\n   const [context, setContext] = useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP' as ProjectContext);\n\n But wait, that doesn't make sense because we are already passing a string.\n\n Actually, the useState hook is generic. We can specify the type like this:\n\n   useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP')\n\n However, in a .tsx file, the angle brackets are not allowed. We must use:\n\n   useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP')   -> This is not allowed in .tsx\n\n Instead, we have to use:\n\n   useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP')   -> but wait, the correct way in .tsx is to use the angle brackets for the generic, but note that the JSX also uses angle brackets.\n\n Actually, in .tsx, we can still use the angle brackets for generics, but we have to be careful.\n\n Alternatively, we can use:\n\n   const [context, setCount] = useState<ProjectContext>();\n   context.current = 'OVERALL_GROUP';\n\n But that is not the way.\n\n The correct way in .tsx is to use the angle brackets for the generic, but note that the JSX might confuse the parser.\n\n However, the TypeScript documentation says that in .tsx files, we must use the `as` keyword for type assertions, but for generic type arguments in function calls, we can still use angle brackets.\n\n But wait, the error we are getting is a syntax error, and it is pointing at the object.\n\n Let me try to change the useState to not use angle brackets.\n\n We can do:\n\n   const [context, setContext] = useState('OVERALL_GROUP') as [ProjectContext, React.Dispatch<React.SetStateAction<ProjectContext>>];\n\n But that is verbose.\n\n Alternatively, we can rely on type inference and not specify the type.\n\n Since we are initializing with a string, and we want the state to be of type ProjectContext, we can do:\n\n   const [context, setContext] = useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP');\n\n But in .tsx, we cannot use the angle brackets because they are confused with JSX.\n\n So we have to use:\n\n   const [context, setContext] = useState<ProjectContext>('OVERALL_GROUP' as any);\n\n But that is not ideal.\n\n Alternatively, we can define the type of the state variable separately.\n\n However, note that the error we are getting is not about the useState line, but about the object.\n\n But let me try to fix the useState by removing the type annotation and letting it infer.\n\n Since we are initializing with a string that is one of the ProjectContext values, and we are not changing the type"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"length","timestamp":1784326589093,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f11b56b5-90b1-427e-804c-4847e5ba72a3"}}
{"type":"compaction","id":"93c9ff77","parentId":"a5ab7997","timestamp":"2026-07-17T22:23:34.449Z","summary":"Let me analyze the conversation to create a structured summary.\n\nFirst, I need to understand what the user is trying to accomplish by reading through the conversation.\n\nLooking at the conversation, I can see it's about:\n1. Clearing cron jobs (initial request)\n2. Creating project brief files in an Obsidian vault\n3. Working on UI design system and color palettes\n4. Configuring Tailwind CSS with specific color tokens\n5. Building a React application (MissionControlLayout) with various components\n6. Splitting the layout into separate files (Sidebar and Canvas components)\n\nThe user has been working on a project called \"WASP Core Update Project\" and specifically on a \"Rhythm Nerve Center\" dashboard.\n\nKey tasks I can identify:\n- Clearing cron jobs (WASP-RESEARCH-OLLAMA and others)\n- Creating 4 markdown brief files for different projects\n- Working on design system tokens (hex colors for UI)\n- Configuring Tailwind.css with specific color palette\n- Building React components for a dashboard layout\n- Recently split the layout into MissionControlSidebar.tsx and MissionControlCanvas.tsx\n\nThe most recent actions show:\n1. Created MissionControlSidebar.tsx successfully\n2. Created MissionControlCanvas.tsx successfully\n\nNow I need to format this into the required structure.\n\n## Goal\nWhat is the user trying to accomplish?\nThe user is building a dashboard application called \"Rhythm Nerve Center\" for the WASP framework. They've been:\n- Clearing background processes\n- Setting up project briefs in an Obsidian vault\n- Implementing a design system with specific color tokens\n- Building a React-based UI with Tailwind CSS\n- Currently working on splitting the layout into modular components (sidebar and canvas)\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\nFrom the conversation, I can identify several constraints:\n- Must use specific hex color codes for the UI design system (provided in the conversation)\n- Must use Tailwind CSS configuration with exact color tokens\n- Must create files at specific paths\n- Must use TypeScript with React\n- Must avoid syntax errors (particularly JSX/TSX parsing issues)\n- Components must follow the exact styling and structure specified\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Cleared cron jobs (WASP-RESEARCH-OLLAMA and others)\n- [x] Created 4 project brief files in the Obsidian vault:\n  - Chief_Madothi_Fund/Brief.md\n  - Defend_Your_Faith_eBooks/Brief.md\n  - Mythology_Subscriptions/Brief.md\n  - STEDT_Tyrone_Commissions/Brief.md\n- [x] Configured Tailwind CSS with the specified color palette\n- [x] Created MissionControlSidebar.tsx component\n- [x] Created MissionControlCanvas.tsx component\n- [x] Set up basic project structure with React/TypeScript\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Finalizing the MissionControlLayout.tsx file that uses the split components\n- [ ] Ensuring the build compiles without errors (previous attempts had syntax errors)\n- [ ] Integrating the sidebar and canvas components into the main layout\n\n### Blocked\n- [Syntax error in page.tsx: \"Unexpected token `div`. Expected jsx identifier\" at line 22]\n- [This appears to be related to TypeScript JSX parsing issues, likely due to angle brackets in type assertions conflicting with JSX syntax]\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **[Use string literals for useState instead of type annotations]**: To avoid TSX parser confusion with angle brackets\n- **[Split layout into separate components]**: To prevent code writing tool from cutting off mid-stream\n- **[Use exact hex color values from design specification]**: To maintain visual consistency with the High Finance palette\n- **[Follow the specified component structure precisely]**: Including class names, layout, and functionality as detailed in directives\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Fix the syntax error in src/app/page.tsx by resolving the TypeScript/JSX conflict (likely by changing useState type assertions)\n2. Import and use the newly created MissionControlSidebar and MissionControlCanvas components in the main layout\n3. Verify the build compiles successfully with pnpm run build\n4. Ensure all components render correctly with the specified design system\n\n## Critical Context\n- File paths referenced:\n  - src/app/page.tsx (main layout file with build errors)\n  - src/components/MissionControlSidebar.tsx (recently created)\n  - src/components/MissionControlCanvas.tsx (recently created)\n  - src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx (referenced but not shown in recent actions)\n- Key functions/components:\n  - MissionControlLayout (main component)\n  - MissionControlSidebar (sidebar navigation)\n  - MissionControlCanvas (main content area)\n  - KanbanBoard (referenced component)\n- Error message: \"Unexpected token `div`. Expected jsx identifier\" at line 22 of page.tsx\n- Color tokens to use:\n  - rhythm-obsidian-deep: #0A0C10\n  - rhythm-charcoal-matte: #12161F\n  - rhythm-glass-specular: #1E2530\n  - rhythm-goldenrod-core: #DAA520\n  - rhythm-gold-liquid: #C5A059\n  - rhythm-silver-mist: #94A3B8\n  - rhythm-sage-metallic: #7A8A80\n  - rhythm-slate-reflection: #334155\n  - rhythm-maroon-depth: #2D1A1E\n- Project contexts:\n  - OVERALL_GROUP\n  - CHIEF_MADOTHI\n  - DEFEND_YOUR_FAITH\n  - MYTHOLOGY_SUBS\n  - STEDT_TYRONE\n- Active screens:\n  - KANBAN\n  - CALENDAR\n  - PROJECTS\n  - BOARDROOM\n  - CAMPAIGNS\n  - OBSIDIAN\n  - PAPERCLIP\n  - SECURITY\n</conversation_summary>\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\nOverwrite `src/app/page.tsx` with the supplied MissionControlLayout code, then run the Next.js build to verify zero compiler warnings and finally output the completion signal “DONE: Core Layout Compiled Cleanly.”\n\n## Early Progress\n- Successfully wrote the new `page.tsx` file (2894 bytes) as instructed.  \n- Executed `pnpm run build`; the build failed with “Module not found” errors for `@/components/MissionControlSidebar` and `@/components/MissionControlCanvas`.\n\n## Context for Suffix\nThe build failure indicates that the referenced component modules are missing or not resolvable under the `@/components` alias. Any subsequent work (the retained suffix) will need to address these missing imports—either by creating the component files, correcting the import paths, or adjusting the alias configuration—before the build can succeed and the completion signal can be issued.\n\n<read-files>\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\components\\Sidebar.js\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\tailwind.config.ts\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\WASP Artwork\\Pallets\\High Finance Palette\\High Finance Assets\\Metalic Palette 1.txt\n</read-files>\n\n<modified-files>\nC:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Chief_Madothi_Fund\\Brief.md\nC:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Defend_Your_Faith_eBooks\\Brief.md\nC:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Mythology_Subscriptions\\Brief.md\nC:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\STEDT_Tyrone_Commissions\\Brief.md\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\app\\globals.css\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\app\\page.tsx\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\KanbanBoard.tsx\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\MissionControlCanvas.tsx\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\MissionControlSidebar.tsx\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\tailwind.config.js\nC:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\tailwind.config.js\n</modified-files>","firstKeptEntryId":"0f132e32","tokensBefore":0,"details":{"readFiles":["C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\components\\Sidebar.js","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\tailwind.config.ts","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\WASP Artwork\\Pallets\\High Finance Palette\\High Finance Assets\\Metalic Palette 1.txt"],"modifiedFiles":["C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Chief_Madothi_Fund\\Brief.md","C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Defend_Your_Faith_eBooks\\Brief.md","C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\Mythology_Subscriptions\\Brief.md","C:\\Users\\MikeT\\Projects\\WASP_Core_Update_Project\\vault\\1_Projects\\STEDT_Tyrone_Commissions\\Brief.md","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\app\\globals.css","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\app\\page.tsx","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\KanbanBoard.tsx","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\MissionControlCanvas.tsx","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\src\\components\\MissionControlSidebar.tsx","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\mission-control-app\\tailwind.config.js","C:\\Warlord_Inc\\Warlord_WASP\\.openclaw\\.openclaw\\workspace\\tailwind.config.js"]},"fromHook":false}
